Acceptance criteria: T03 mechanical acceptance met.
  - AC-1 happy path; AC-3 and AC-4 anti-drift (the slip is compared to
    T4SlipParser's own output property by property by reflection, with a guard
    that the walk saw all 30 properties; the mapping is compared to
    T4LineMapper's own output entry by entry - line, amount, source box codes -
    plus UnmappedBoxCodes).
  - AC-5 attribution echoed ordinally and untrimmed for all five caller strings
    plus the tax year; AC-6 UnmappedBoxCodes sequence-equal to the mapper's and
    never rejecting; AC-8 result year coherence.
  - AC-24 empty box list yields the parser's required-box errors; AC-25 zero
    amounts; AC-26 required boxes only; AC-27 half-cent boundary equals
    MoneyRounding.ToCents (100.005 -> 100.01, 100.015 -> 100.02) on both the slip
    and every line entry Box 14 feeds; AC-28 no arithmetic - an executable-line
    scan of all five production files finds no MoneyRounding, Math.Round,
    MidpointRounding, double, float, or even a `decimal` token, with a scanner
    guard proving the walk saw every file.
  - AC-9 null extraction (exactly one error, no throw); AC-10 GenericEvidence
    kind with the provider never queried; AC-11 at pipeline level; stage 3+4
    accumulation proved to emit TaxYear before PayloadBoxes.
  - AC-14 through AC-21: all eight parser rejection families (duplicate box,
    missing Box 12/45/54, malformed amount, negative amount, constrained code out
    of range, missing companion box) each assert the result's errors are
    sequence-equal to T4SlipParser's own errors for the same payload - verbatim
    and in order - with the provider never queried.
  - AC-22 provider failure surfaced verbatim and in order (a two-error stub pins
    ordering) with no other year requested; AC-23 a recording provider proves
    TryGetForYear was never called on parser rejection.
  - AC-34 policy is exactly [2025] in one place; AC-35 the provider is asked for
    2025 exactly once and it is the slip's year; AC-36 a provider holding only
    2024 never hands its map to a 2025 slip (MapWasHandedOut stays false);
    AC-37 2024 and 2026 envelopes never become a ValidatedExtraction and neither
    year is coerced.
  - Unsupported extraction years (2024, 2026, 1999) fail closed with a single
    TaxYear error and no provider query. These are built through the internal
    ValidatedExtraction constructor by reflection because spec 007 will not mint
    one - which is precisely why stage 3 must be provable on its own rather than
    leaning on the upstream gate.
  - Every failure across an 11-case corpus carries no value and throws nothing;
    every self-originated Field is a T4ProcessingFields constant; this module's
    own messages are non-interpolated constants naming no year; neither the
    extraction nor its payload is mutated.
Decisions flagged for one-pass human override:
  [ASSUMED] Stage 2 is sequential, not accumulating: a non-T4 extraction
  correctly carries no payload (spec 007 forbids one), so also reporting
  "a T4 payload is required" would invent a defect that is not there.
  architecture.md states stage 2 as one rule yielding "error(s)", which permits
  either reading.
Known coverage gap, deliberate and recorded:
  Stage 6 (slip/extraction year mismatch) is implemented but currently
  unreachable - SupportedProcessingTaxYears is [2025] and T4SlipParser yields
  2025 only, so a slip that parses cannot disagree with an extraction that
  reached stage 6. There is therefore no live rejection test for it. Instead
  SlipYearGuard_IsUnreachableOnlyBecauseBothYearPoliciesAgree pins the property
  that makes it unreachable and fails the moment either policy widens, at which
  point stage 6 needs a live arm.
Mutation evidence (the arms are not vacuous):
  - Re-word engine errors instead of surfacing them verbatim -> 10 tests fail.
  - Retry an adjacent year when the provider fails -> 3 tests fail.
  - Drop the stage-4 structural guard -> 4 tests fail, including the
    ArgumentNullException from T4SlipParser's GroupBy that the guard exists to
    prevent.
  - Drop the unsupported-year check -> 4 tests fail.
  - Accept a non-T4 kind -> 1 test fails.
  - Trim attribution on the way out -> 1 test fails.
  - On parser failure, map a stand-in slip anyway -> 9 tests fail.
  - SURVIVED: invoking the mapper with an empty slip list on the parser-failure
    path. T4LineMapper rejects an empty list before querying the provider, so the
    call has no observable effect and no tax consequence. T4LineMapper is
    constructed internally by design, so "the mapper was not invoked" is
    observable only through the provider; every parser-rejection arm asserts the
    provider was never queried, and the stand-in-slip mutation above shows that
    assertion bites for any invocation carrying a real slip.
